  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "```"
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "They were led through silent, gleaming streets."
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "The Solantri they passed stopped to watch, their light-pulses flickering in patterns too fast for Geralt to follow, but he felt the applicator in his head twitch, attempting to parse them."
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo Crown was the city’s heart: a vast, natural amphitheater open to the sky, at its center a single, massive tuning fork of the same pearlescent material, three stories tall."
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "Around it, on concentric rings of stone, sat the city’s council."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "Their light was steadier, deeper in hue."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "The lead councillor’s voice resonated in the hollow space. “I am Elara."
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "We monitor the Spire’s dreams."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "For ten thousand years, they were the same: a memory of light, and a command to sleep."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "Now, the dreams are changing."
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "They are becoming… screams."
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "Lentharis, our Keeper, wakes in fear."
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "And the Proto-Dracos, who have been our peaceful, simple neighbors since the Sundering, are becoming agitated."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "They gather."
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "They move with purpose."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "They are drawn to the Spire, and we do not know why.”"
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "“Drawn how?” Oreck asked, his voice echoing in the space."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "“As if called."
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "But we hear nothing."
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "Our communications are light."
  - line: 145
    type: narration
    text: "Theirs are… something else."
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "Something older."
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "And now, you arrive."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "Your resonance is loud."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "It shakes the ash.”"
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "A younger Solantri, standing at the edge of the council ring, stepped forward."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "His name-pulse came through as Kethran."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "His light was a sharper, more inquisitive blue."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "He stared directly at Geralt, his head tilted."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "“Your resonance is… layered,” Kethran said, his harmonic voice curious. “I hear the Anchor’s bond."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "The Architect’s echo."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "And beneath it… a whisper."
  - line: 159
    type: narration
    text: "An echo that does not belong."
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "A frequency that is answering a call we cannot hear.”"
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt a cold trickle down his spine. “My applicator?”"
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "“No."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "Something using your applicator."
  - line: 166
    type: narration
    text: "A sympathetic vibration."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "It is faint, but it is there."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "And it is growing.”"
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Before Geralt could respond, a series of sharp, crimson light-pulses flashed from the city walls—an alarm."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "A guard’s voice resonated, tight with panic. “The Proto-Dracos!"
  - line: 173
    type: narration
    text: "Hundreds of them!"
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "Massing at the western approach!"
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "They… they are not shambling."
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "They are marching!”"
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "Elara’s light dimmed with dread. “It has begun."
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "Kethran, take them to the Underchamber."
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "Find the source of this call."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "We will hold the walls.”"
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "Kethran gestured urgently. “This way."
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "Quickly.”"

